SEC. 51P-946.109. YARD, LOT, AND SPACE REGULATIONS.

(Note: The yard, lot, and space regulations in this section must be read together with the yard, lot, and space regulations in Division 51A-4.400. If there is a conflict between this section and Division 51A-4.400, this section controls.)

(a) In general. Except as provided in this section, the yard, lot, and space regulations for the MF-1(A) Multifamily District apply.

(b) Multifamily use.

(1) Front yard.

(A) Minimum front yard is 15 feet.

(B) Balconies, bay windows, awnings, and signs affixed to the building or part of the foundation may project up to five feet into the required front yard, if the minimum clearance of the projection is 12 feet above grade.

(C) Stoops, steps, patios, stairs, planters, retaining walls, transformers and other utility equipment, benches, pots, raised planters, sculptures, cabanas, and other decorative landscape items may be located within the required front yard.

(2) Side yard. Minimum side yard is 15 feet.

(3) Density. Maximum number of dwelling units is 122.

(4) Height.

(A) Except as provided in Subparagraphs (B) and (C), maximum structure height is 45 feet, measured to the top of the multifamily use.

(B) Except as provided in Subparagraph (C), maximum structure height within the easternmost 35 feet of the Property is 36 feet, measured to the top of the multifamily use.

(C) The roof and the following structures may project up to a total height of 58 feet above grade, measured to the highest point:

(i) elevator penthouse or bulkhead;

(ii) mechanical equipment room;

(iii) cooling tower;

(iv) tank designed to hold liquids;

(v) ornamental cupola or dome;

(vi) skylights;

(vii) clerestory;

(viii) visual screens which surround roof mounted mechanical equipment;

(ix) chimney and vent stacks;

(x) amateur communications tower;

(xi) parapet wall; and

(xii) storage areas.

(D) The residential proximity slope regulations in Section 51A-4.412 do not apply to this district.

(5) Lot coverage. Maximum lot coverage is 65 percent. Aboveground parking structures are included in lot coverage calculations; surface parking lots and underground parking structures are not.

(6) Lot size. For a multifamily use, no minimum lot size is required.

(7) Stories.

(A) Except as provided in this subsection, maximum number of stories above grade is four.

(B) Maximum number of stories within the easternmost 35 feet of the Property is three. (Ord. 29936)
